	* trunk/wvstreams/linuxstreams/wvipaliaser.cc: WvIPAliaser::add()
	  would get confused when handling an IP address, if an alias had
	  already been added for it. So, it would decide that this address
	  was already handled by a real interface and decrement that alias'
	  reference-count. Now we make sure to ignore any interface aliases,
	  when determining whether an IP address is a local interface.
