	  anymore, relying on closecallbacks to tell us when we're done. But
	  there was a couple of places in WvHTTPStream where we were setting
	  the 'cloned' pointer directly instead of calling setclone(), which
	  is what sets the closecallback in the first place. Short version
	  of the story: softupdate works again now.

