	  trunk/wvstreams/uniconf/uniinigen.cc,
	  trunk/wvstreams/urlget/tests/http2test.cc,
	  trunk/wvstreams/urlget/wvftpstream.cc,
	  trunk/wvstreams/urlget/wvhttpstream.cc: Using getline() with a
	  non-zero timeout is fundamentally evil, but when you need it, you
	  do need it. What to do? Enter Guilt-Oriented Orthodontic
	  Programming (also known as GOOP). Renamed getline() to
	  blocking_getline(), and put a short inline getline() that does not
	  have the timeout parameter at all and calls blocking_getline()
	  with a zero timeout. This way, you can still specify a non-zero
	  timeout if you need to, but you'll be guilt-ridden by the
	  obviously evil function you'll be using. Also, it's more easily
	  greppable, so we can find offenders quicker and fix them.

