	  trunk/wvstreams/utils/tests/ondisklisttest.cc,
	  trunk/wvstreams/utils/tests/ondiskspeedtest.cc,
	  trunk/wvstreams/utils/tests/qdbmtest.cc,
	  trunk/wvstreams/utils/wvbdbhash.cc,
	  trunk/wvstreams/utils/wvgdbmhash.cc,
	  trunk/wvstreams/utils/wvqdbmhash.cc,
	  trunk/wvstreams/utils/wvstringlist.cc,
	  trunk/wvstreams/utils/wvtask.cc, trunk/wvstreams/vars.mk: Added
	  mag's changes to WvBdbHash and WvOnDiskHash. This means we now use
	  a templated class called WvOnDiskHash (to which you pass the dbm
	  implementation that you want) instead of using WvBdbHash directly.
	  WvOnDiskHash allows for more portable code since the program
	  doesn't have to explicitly know what hash its using. In the future
	  we could easily port other dbm implementations (e.g., djb's cdm)
	  with much ease. Also, WvGdbmHash has been ripped out and replaced
	  with WvQdbmHash. qdbm is an LGPL dbm that is (supposedly) faster
	  than gdm. BUGZID: 3021

