	  trunk/wvstreams/streams/wvstreamclone.h,
	  trunk/wvstreams/streams/wvstreamlist.cc: WvStream::Callback
	  functions now all return void -- no one ever used the return
	  values anyway. A new virtual function, WvStream::execute(), is
	  used if no callback is defined. That way, derived classes can
	  simply override execute() instead of fiddling with static member
	  functions and other uglies.

